<title>MEXICO: Two Mexican ports close due to bad weather.</title>
<headline>Two Mexican ports close due to bad weather.</headline>
<dateline>MEXICO CITY 1997-04-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>Mexican authorities closed the Gulf of Mexico ports of Tampico and Altamira on Saturday because of strong winds, the government news agency Notimex reported.</p>
<p>Fishing boats had been warned since Friday not to sail because of choppy seas, Notimex said, citing the Regional Port Captaincy in the city of Tampico on the gulf coast.</p>
<p>Tampico is one of Mexico's main export ports for petroleum, grains and other products headed for the southern United States.</p>
<p>--Dan Trotta, Mexico City newsroom, +525 728-9507</p>
